decide to stay in America.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.570
And what I mean by that is it's obviously

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:34.020
an older country for that
point, but there's a,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.030
there an incredible thing that Sweden has

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.300
that I admire, which is socially,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.310
it's so outrageously
progressive in comparison

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.160
to the macro world.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:49.160
However, it's not as
foofy foofy or soft or

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.670
becomes the cliche, you
know, ideological thing.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:55.830
There's still an incredible
level of practicality,

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.600
innovation, entrepreneurship.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:02.270
I guess ultimately, I admire the balance

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:07.270
of the business culture
human infrastructure

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:13.300
and so, yeah, I've always
felt, you know, it's funny.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.490
I like to keep things basic.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.933
But we spelled good when I was here.

